        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-10-29T23:50:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So, I just want to sanity check something.<br>\n<code>Push Your Limits (I): You have no limit on amount of Reactions you can take. Each time you use a Reaction after the first one each turn, take 1 irreducible damage or take a minor twist.</code><br>\n<code>Untouchable (R): When you would be dealt damage, roll a while in the Green zone, while in the Yellow, or while in Red. Reduce the damage you take by the value rolled. Attack another target with that roll.</code><br>\nIf you somehow end up in a situation where you take damage from Push Your Limits, can Untouchable be used in reaction to the 1 irreducible damage?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:26.446Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
