      {
        "id": 234108,
        "name": "der andere Jan",
        "username": "der_andere_Jan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-10-30T19:11:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"catDreaming\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> catDreaming:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I  accidentally  built a character with these two abilities on their sheet when the first draft of the core rulebook released, and you can see them in the Rate My Build thread as the very first submission. I wasn’t intending for it; It just kinda happened. I didn’t realize that this combo was a thing until yesterday shortly before I opened this thread.</p>\n<p>Edit: The character in question is also extremely unlikely to use this combo, despite it being an option for them, so maybe that’s what you were meaning?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Oops, my bad. I mixed this up with the combo on ‘push your limits’ + ‘like the wind’ that came up later in the rate my build thread, and which was more of an exercise in how OP we can get. <span class=\"bbcode-i\">That</span> combo, while technically allowed by the RAW, requires an ‘the ancient relic made me a futuristic cyborg’ - type contradictory backstory*, and that was what I had in mind here.<br>\nSo, apologies for the confusion about that point!</p>\n<p>*There is, of course, the Guyver manga/movies; so anyone is free to argue I am completely wrong about this being contradictory anyway <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:06.772Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 18,
        "readers_count": 17,
        "score": 8.6,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 20362,
        "topic_slug": "untouchable-push-your-limits-clarification",
        "display_username": "der andere Jan",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"catDreaming\"]\n\nI  accidentally  built a character with these two abilities on their sheet when the first draft of the core rulebook released, and you can see them in the Rate My Build thread as the very first submission. I wasn't intending for it; It just kinda happened. I didn't realize that this combo was a thing until yesterday shortly before I opened this thread.\n\nEdit: The character in question is also extremely unlikely to use this combo, despite it being an option for them, so maybe that's what you were meaning?\n\n[/quote]\n\nOops, my bad. I mixed this up with the combo on 'push your limits' + 'like the wind' that came up later in the rate my build thread, and which was more of an exercise in how OP we can get. [i]That[/i] combo, while technically allowed by the RAW, requires an 'the ancient relic made me a futuristic cyborg' - type contradictory backstory*, and that was what I had in mind here.\nSo, apologies for the confusion about that point!\n\n*There is, of course, the Guyver manga/movies; so anyone is free to argue I am completely wrong about this being contradictory anyway :)",
