        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/justindoodler/{size}/4832_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-05-07T20:04:53.715Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I would say that these don’t combo. Being “dealt” damage is not the same as taking damage. Essentially  the Irreducible damage from Push your limits is a cost for taking extra reactions, but it’s not “dealt” to you from , say an attacker. The same for trying to combo Push your limit with other abilities triggered by being “dealt” damage.</p>",
